3280-i20220104-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-747-1309-c","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-133280-i20220104","date":"2022-01-04","original_code":"747.1309(c)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-01-18","finding":"Primary Caregiver Annual Training - Special topics for children under 24 months: One out of one employee records did not have child maltreatment, SIDS, shaken baby, early brain development, administering medication, and food allergy training on file. There were 22 out of 30 hours for the annual 2020-2021 year.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026506900","violation_type_title":"Primary Caregiver Annual Training - Special topics for children under 24 months (26 TAC §747.1309(c))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-133280-i20220104-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-747-5417-a-2","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-133280-i20220104","date":"2022-01-04","original_code":"747.5417(a)(2)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-01-10","finding":"Required Equipment in Vehicles - Emergency Medical Information: The provider did not have emergency medical authorization for 1 child  who requires transportation. There were also 2 children on file who required transportation that did not have transportation authorization. Two other children who accompany the provider to pick up the school-age children also did not have the required authorization for transportation.","topic":"fire","source_record_id":"1026346522","violation_type_title":"Required Equipment in Vehicles - Emergency Medical Information (26 TAC §747.5417(a)(2))","topic_label":"Fire safety & emergency drills"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-133280-i20220104-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-747-3203","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-133280-i20220104","date":"2022-01-04","original_code":"747.3203","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":